---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import FundRepeater from '../components/FundRepeater.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Our Network" description="A community radio network, built by volunteers and powered by the sun, that helps Western New Yorkers stay in touch when other systems are down.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Our network"
    title="A network built by neighbors"
    intro="Small radios, solar power, and a lot of help from the community. Here's what it is and how you can be part of it."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        Our community network is a web of small, low-power radios spread across Western New York.
        Each one can pass a short text message along to the next, so a message can travel across
        town and beyond without cell towers, internet, or the power grid.
      </p>
      <p>
        A backbone of repeaters on tall buildings, towers, and other high places carries messages
        across the region. Many run on solar panels and batteries, so they keep working through an
        outage. We build these backbone sites together with local businesses and organizations.
        Each one costs about ${site.repeaters.cost} to build. About {site.repeaters.regionTotal} are on the air across the region,
        built by community members and by WNYMesh ({site.repeaters.deployed} so far).
        <a href="#fund">Help fund the next one</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        With so many people joining, we're focusing our resources on high sites that serve whole
        communities, so we generally aren't able to place repeaters at private homes. Want better coverage
        where you live? You can set up your own node, and our community on
        <a href={site.networkSite.url}>{site.networkSite.name}</a> and Discord is happy to help.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it's for</h2>
      <p>
        Everyone. Families checking on each other after a storm, neighbors looking out for one
        another, and community groups that want a dependable backup. You don't need a license or
        a technical background to use it.
      </p>

      <div class="notice">
        <p>The network is a community backup for staying in touch. It is not monitored by emergency services. <strong>Always call 911 in an emergency if you can.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-badge"><Icon name="radio" /></div>
          <h3>Join the network</h3>
          <p>
            Our network currently runs on a system called MeshCore. Everything you need to get
            started, including which radio to get, setup guides, the coverage map, and our friendly
            Discord community, is on our network site.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href={site.radioGuideUrl}>Which radio to get</a>
            <a class="btn btn--soft" href={site.networkSite.url}>Visit {site.networkSite.name}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-badge"><Icon name="home" /></div>
          <h3>Partner on a backbone site</h3>
          <p>
            Own or manage a tall building, a tower, or high ground with a wide view? A backbone
            repeater there can keep whole communities connected. We'd love to talk.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--soft" href="/partners/#backbone">Talk to us about a site</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="fund">
    <div class="container narrow"><FundRepeater /></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
